@startuml DashboardDelivery
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: deliver same-directory sandbox instances and the native Proveo dashboard
' status: PLANNED. The tmux baselines in D0 run today. D1–D7 are implementation gates.
' UI reference: _spec/_experiments/dashboard/index.html (Review queue, lower-right split)
' Runtime design: _spec/_experiments/dashboard/workspace-instances.puml
' Admission design: _spec/_experiments/dashboard/resource-queue.puml and resource_queue.qnt
' Current runtime: _spec/internal/sbx/{instance-lifecycle,state-sync,clone-workspace,kit-lifecycle}.puml
' Supersedes the proposed 1:1 ownership and shared writable history in
' _spec/_plans/session-continuity.puml.
'
' D0  BASELINE AND STOCK SBX PROBE
' Record the existing CLI, state formats and tmux visuals before changing
' default dispatch. On each supported sbx host, pin the sbx version and run
' its stock interactive entry point from a fixed-size tmux pane. Capture an
' empty inventory and a seeded card, including cursor, footer and colors.
' Determine the supported inventory ID, usage and disk setting outputs and
' units. Confirm whether child TUI exit stops only the client. Find the sbx
' storage filesystem and confirm how disk reservations become observable.
' Test the adapters against those observations before consuming their output.
' The checked-in sbx-dashboard.png shows sbx v0.23.0 and is a composition
' reference for the dark background, flat dividers and key-first footer.
' Compare live stock and embedded sbx on the same pinned version and grid.
'
' D0 MEASURED 2026-11-24 (Linux arm64, tmux 3.7b, Go 1.26.10)
' e2e/dashboard_tmux_test.go captures the real post-exit card in a 120×40
' pane. The card spans 37×11 cells. Its gray (#8A8A8A) frame and footer
' rule, cyan (#00BAC6) selected face, dark teal (#0E3A48) idle face and
' selected-only ↵ match the pattern in the Chromium attach prototype.
' The native card has rounded cell corners and uses the terminal background.
' The prototype uses a rectangular border and dimmed backdrop. Use the
' native card geometry and identity styles for Attach.
' Chromium verified that the prototype holds the outer frame at 1160×810
' pixels across tabs, focuses Cancel, moves ↵ with focus, and restores
' the selected task's focus after simulated detach. This is the HTML sample.
' The real proveo attach command accepted keys and returned with the same
' agent pane still alive after Ctrl+B d or Ctrl+B L, respectively.
' TestDashboardRunsThreeTasksFromOneDirectoryOnTmux submits three prompts
' from e2e/testdata/_spec/_plans/ into one workdir. It checks
' overlapping pane lifetimes, prompt routing and separate run outcomes.
' The fixture workers share the host directory.
' [Unverified] Live sbx parity, disk settings and telemetry on the daemon
' host. The Linux verification environment has no sbx binary or daemon.
'
' D1  INSTANCE IDENTITY, PRIVATE WORK, SAFE MIGRATION
' Runtime implemented. The live three-VM acceptance gate is pending.
' Touch cmd/proveo run, lifecycle verbs and clean, internal/run,
' internal/sbx inventory, internal/backend/sandbox receipts and teardown,
' internal/proveohome, schedule selectors, and the defs workspace contract.
' Resolve one canonical effective pwd for all defs. Honor --input / --scope
' and carry the resolved guest cwd independently of image WORKDIR, Git
' source, build paths and harness home. Ignore symlink aliases of that pwd.
' Store workspace -> instances, with immutable instance and attempt IDs.
' Put a task label and Git base on the record. Allocate agent-task-shortid
' within 32 ASCII chars. Use adhoc without a ticket and reserve the suffix
' before clipping the task slug. Handle a name collision before creating.
' Store the owning host, inventory VM ID and launch receipt. Keep the name
' stable across edits to a task title. Reuse needs matching identity and
' create-time settings, a verified idle state and an acquired owner lease.
' Serialize launch through settling and lifecycle verbs per instance.
' Reconciliation distinguishes matching, stale, missing and unknown VMs.
' Failed listing means unknown. Never mutate a VM based on name alone.
' A live external owner needs an explicit recovery path. Pin backing paths
' while a VM may depend on them. Keep and Cancel is the safe replacement
' answer. Replace and Continue carries only the selected instance first.
' Migrate each trusted legacy (pwd, target) record into one default
' instance without renaming its VM or rewriting its history. Keep discovery
' of legacy records while readers roll forward. Quarantine ambiguous
' records for operator selection. Keep migration repeatable and reversible
' through a legacy index backup. Clean follows migrated ownership and skips
' unknown resources. Preserve browser profile and port ownership rules.
' CLI: run <target> --new [--task ...] and run <target> --instance ID.
' Keep the implicit single candidate. With several, pick interactively or
' report a required selector. --continue resumes the chosen native ID.
' Scheduled jobs pin an instance or request a new one.
' Create one private guest checkout and feature branch per instance from a
' recorded commit. Bundle a base missing from the remote. Leave host edits
' in place unless an explicit snapshot includes them. Isolate non-Git paths
' with a private copy. Guard writable direct mode against overlapping paths.
' Gate: e2e/dashboard_instances_sbx_test.go launches three instances of the
' same target concurrently from one real pwd. Assert distinct VM IDs, guest
' files, branch refs and outputs. Confirm host edits stay unchanged. Attempt
' a duplicate owner, simulate stale and unknown inventory in adapter tests,
' and show that cleanup or replacement touches only its elected instance.
' Reuse e2e/clone_test.go for host/worktree compatibility.
'
' D2  HISTORY ON THE HOST THAT OWNS THE VM
' Touch internal/backend/sandbox teardown, result carry and harness state,
' internal/sbx state export and internal/proveohome resume. Read attempt
' receipts for recovery after a runner restarts. Run a managed checkpoint at
' exit after success, failure, interruption or requested stop. Keep
' checkpoint and Git carry outcomes separate and visible.
' Export a consistent native checkpoint to private staging, validate its
' native session ID and payload, sync it and atomically publish it. Advance
' the instance head only after publication. Retries are idempotent. Resume
' the chosen native ID from a clean VM and carried Git ref. Keep live locks,
' sockets and authentication material outside the archive.
' Try periodic safe checkpoints where the harness supports them. A full
' disk, failed permissions, unreachable guest, abrupt host death or raw sbx
' removal can prevent final export. Preserve the last good checkpoint and
' record a recovery reason. Keep a surviving VM through failed history or
' Git carry unless the operator explicitly discards it. Reconcile raw sbx
' stop/removal without asserting a new session checkpoint exists.
' Prove native restore for each supported harness and pin capabilities by
' version. Scope Claude Code projects/session records to the instance.
' Check Codex rollout/SQLite requirements and Cursor's native restore.
' Use a per-instance Hermes home to isolate the DB and gateway. Keep
' unsupported restore visibly unavailable. Publish only verified history.
' Gate: add e2e/dashboard_history_sbx_test.go. Exit two same-pwd instances
' in both orders, then resume each by exact native ID in a rebuilt VM.
' Verify cancellation, failed export, retry, retained VM and raw removal.
' Inject read/write failures outside sbx at the adapter boundary. Inspect
' artifacts for excluded paths. Reuse e2e/resume_test.go.
'
' D3  OPENCODE HISTORY FIX (OWN PR, CAN PROCEED BESIDE D1)
' Reproduce lost history on the pinned OpenCode version, including its
' project filter on guest cwd changes. Verify a native export/import round
' trip across rebuilt VMs and changed paths, including messages and child
' sessions. Preserve the native ID. Keep engine backups private and check
' that portable archives exclude credentials. Preserve the existing engine
' while migration remains unverified. Test retained and replaced engines
' with e2e/opencode_engine_sbx_test.go. D2 can ship per harness while this
' fix lands separately. OpenCode joins the portable-resume matrix after D3.
'
' D4  RESOURCE-DRIVEN ADMISSION
' Touch internal/schedule, internal/sbx host capacity and the run launch
' boundary shared by calendar, manual and retry paths. Calendar submits
' a durable item. The headless scheduler owns dispatch and recovers
' pending work on restart. Submission, carry, prerequisite completion
' and changes from a bounded disk probe wake it. Closing the dashboard
' leaves queued and running work with the scheduler.
' Implement Queued → Reserved → Running → Settling → Attention required
' in Go. Model acceptance, invalid requests, failed start, retry and
' reconciliation as explicit events. Persist state and leases before
' launch. Serialize admissions across Proveo queues on the owning host.
' Synchronous run acquires the same lease or reports why it cannot launch.
' Reserve disk for new VMs only. An already-accounted VM keeps its own charge.
' Read sbx settings get sandbox.disk.dockerVolume on the owning host.
' Display the configured value verbatim and record its byte equivalent with
' the lease. Use the smaller of policy and actual filesystem headroom.
' Prevent counting an allocation twice when it starts appearing in samples.
' Retain pending leases across unknown inventory and through settling.
' Reconcile charges on restart and resample before reusing freed headroom.
' Keep CPU and system RAM as telemetry. Show discrete VRAM separately and
' count unified memory once. Show one segment per 2 CPU cores, 8 GiB RAM
' and 64 GiB disk, with occupied capacity and muted totals.
' Show a wait reason for stale, unreadable or insufficient disk and for
' unmet dependencies. Pick the oldest ready item that fits. Do not promise
' dispatch times. Keep deadlines for job budgets and sample freshness.
' Gate: keep Go transitions aligned with the Quint cases. Test competing
' reservers, restarts, stale samples, changed settings, and full disks with
' injected capacity. Add e2e/dashboard_admission_test.go for concurrent
' CLI producers and reconciliation. Use a disposable sbx host to verify
' the configured disk value and the observe/start/carry/release cycle.
'
' D5  TASK READ MODEL AND HANDOFF
' Join task source, initial prompt, agent, instance, attempt, carried Git
' refs, review revision and scheduler state. Begin with local _plan/ files
' and explicit ticket references. Resolve GitHub/GitLab separately from
' the task source. Add provider reads to show linked ticket excerpt, PR and
' push timestamps when available. Keep reads cached and failure-tolerant.
' Detect missing IDs and cycles before dispatch. Keep blocker identifiers
' visible when a graph row folds. Record stable order and keep the stable
' job selector used by attach.
' Keep task phase separate from capacity. Track spec → verification → spec
' → live verification (repeat) → upgrade → PR → review → merge. Review
' feedback can requeue work. Mark results and verification with the exact
' revision. A new revision reopens affected verification. Support overnight
' submission and daytime review through the same records. Leave PR and
' merge posting with the operator.
' Read Changes from the recorded base and carried tip, including deleted
' and renamed files. Retain the reachable objects during review. Display
' last known revision and age or pending carry for live work. Use a separate
' read-only Files view anchored to pwd. Show deleted contents from the base
' and changed contents from the tip. Confine host file reads to effective
' pwd, including symlink resolution.
' Gate: fixture tests cover selection, stale provider reads, dependency
' cycles, revision-driven rework and diff paths with rename/delete.
'
' D6  NATIVE TERMINAL AND CHILD OWNERSHIP
' Add a Go dashboard model, reuse choiceui, internal/ui and ptyproxy.
' Bubble Tea v2 owns terminal input and the alternate screen. Lip Gloss v2
' composes the panes and Bubbles v2 provides the key-map footer. Reuse
' creack/pty and x/term on Unix. Qualify Charm x/vt with live sbx before
' pinning it for grid, cursor, scrollback, terminal replies and resize.
' Start native sbx at the content pane size on entry to its tab, and keep
' the client across view switches. Render stock cells and the stock footer
' inside the pane. The Proveo multiplexer owns only its global chrome and
' keys. Show effective pwd, proveo/sbx tabs and Ctrl+G then Tab in the
' header. Preserve both views' dimensions and state through switches.
' Forward child input, paste and mouse, except reserved parent sequences.
' Forward an unmatched Ctrl+G prefix after a bounded wait or next key.
' Ctrl+C on either tab and SIGINT use bounded parent shutdown, return 130,
' restore the terminal and leave jobs/VMs alone. Reap a dashboard-owned
' child client. If it exits, show status in Proveo without a shell fallback.
' Preserve headless help and --help. Show the sbx view as unavailable when
' the client, daemon or qualified PTY is missing. Verify Windows still
' builds with the PTY fallback.
' Port Review queue with lower-right split first. Use Attention required,
' Working and Queued with an outlined n new instance item under Queued.
' Port Task graph with bounded path folding (for example, "3 tasks").
' Port Schedule with wait reasons and completed runs. Offer alternate
' detail placement via Task detail options. Keep the demo chooser outside
' the terminal reference.
' Preserve column layout at narrow widths. Clip at cell boundaries and let
' panes scroll independently. Reuse the sbx background (#1B1B20), identity
' colors and key-first muted action hints. Use red D and strike for deletes.
' Show CPU, RAM and disk usage before task details. Query the selected
' sandbox on selection and every 5s while visible. Use one bounded request,
' discard stale replies, show unknown values and retain a dated last sample.
' Show the Git + task source, ticket, branch, instance, sandbox, PR,
' three-row excerpt, muted last-pushed date/time and original prompt.
' t toggles detail. f/g switch Files/Changes. ↵ on a file opens its preview
' across the task and detail panes. e opens Fresh only inside the selected
' running guest via sbx exec on its owning host, in the recorded guest cwd
' as its run user. Hide e if the guest or editor is unavailable.
' Enter on a live task confirms via the existing card style. Name the agent
' and task, default to Cancel and recheck the job before proveo attach.
' Suspend terminal drawing for direct attachment or hand off the tmux client
' that invoked it. Ctrl+B d detaches direct attach. Ctrl+B L switches back
' from an existing tmux client. The attached agent receives its own input.
' Restore selection, focus and scroll in both cases.
' New instance wizard confirms agent, optional task, name and opening prompt.
' Submit the wizard's snapshot through the same runner as CLI and schedule.
' Gate: add e2e/dashboard_native_tmux_test.go for bare CLI, all views, wizard,
' attach/cancel/detach, details, diff and guest-only Fresh. Exercise two
' tmux clients to verify which one attach switches. Drive 120×40, 80×24
' and a live resize. Test ANSI cells, clipping, keys and pane state.
' Add e2e/dashboard_sbx_tmux_test.go for stock vs embedded text and styles,
' cursor and replies, live switch preservation, and Ctrl+C on both tabs.
' Compare the embedded viewport with direct sbx at identical dimensions
' and seed. Mask only measured volatile cells such as elapsed times.
' Assert exit 130, restored modes, no fallback shell and a surviving job.
'
' D7  RELEASE GATE
' Land in dependency order as reviewable PRs. D1 is first runtime ownership.
' D2 and D4 build on it. D5 joins D1/D2/D4. D6 can prototype on fixed
' fixtures early, then connects the verified runtime. D3 stays separate.
' Keep bare proveo help until native checks pass. Publish migration notes
' and repair commands for orphaned and legacy records. Keep existing
' selectors readable during rollback. Never roll back by deleting sessions.
' Each slice updates its current-state _spec, adds its named E2E checks,
' runs unit/contract tests, go vet and PlantUML, and records skip reasons.
' Run tmux checks on Linux and macOS. Run live sbx gates on a supported
' daemon host. A prerequisite skip leaves a release gate pending.

title PLANNED — Native dashboard and same-directory sandboxes

component "D0\nCapture current behavior" as D0 <<host>>
component "D1\nInstance identity and private checkout" as D1 <<app>>
component "D2\nNative history and resume" as D2 <<db>>
component "D3\nOpenCode history PR" as D3 <<app>>
queue "D4\nDisk admission" as D4 <<async>>
component "D5\nTask and Git read model" as D5 <<app>>
component "D6\nNative dashboard and sbx tab" as D6 <<app>>
component "D7\nRelease gates" as D7 <<host>>

D0 ARROW_MAIN D1
D0 ARROW_OPTIONAL D3
D1 ARROW_MAIN D2
D1 ARROW_QUEUE D4
D2 ARROW_MAIN D5
D4 ARROW_QUEUE D5
D5 ARROW_MAIN D6
D3 ARROW_MAIN D7
D6 ARROW_MAIN D7
@enduml
